{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessFinal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessFinal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessFinal.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_stripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessFinal.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_stripGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdUniquenessFinal.lean#L36-L62","doc":"**`phiBProd` uniqueness up to scalar (substrate, `hΦ₂_iso` discharged).** For the physical\nsubstrate `Φ_b = phiBProd (substrateB t)` (`t > 0`): any `FaddeevPhi` solution `Φ₁` that is\n`FaddeevPhiStripGrowth` (comparable to `phiBProd`), with the normal-form identity off\n`phiBProd`'s zeros and the two dense periodicity loci, is proportional to `phiBProd`. Both the\n`hbdd` growth bound and `phiBProd`'s zero isolation are internalized as theorems. ","signatureChunk":0}]}